lesson: 148
title: The area of a shape made of rectangles
level: primary-3
stars: 2
explain: An L-shaped figure can be seen in two ways: as two rectangles side by side, or as a big rectangle with a corner cut away.
explain: A 10 by 8 rectangle with a 4 by 3 corner cut away has area 10 × 8 - 4 × 3 = 80 - 12 = 68.
explain: Cut it into two rectangles instead, 10 by 5 and 6 by 3: 50 + 18 = 68, the same. Careful: the perimeter of such an L is still 2 × (10 + 8) = 36, the cut corner does not change it.
vars: a=name W=6..20 H=5..18 w=2..9 h=2..9
need: w < W && h < H
answer: W * H - w * h
exercise: A {w} cm by {h} cm rectangle is cut out of one corner of a {W} cm by {H} cm rectangle. What is the area of the shape that is left, in square centimetres?
exercise: An L-shaped garden is made of two rectangles: one is {W} m by {H-h} m, the other is {W-w} m by {h} m. What is the area of the garden in square metres?
exercise: A shape is made of two rectangles that do not overlap: one is {w} cm by {H-h} cm and the other is {W-w} cm by {H} cm. Find the area of the shape in square centimetres.
exercise: A room is {W} m by {H} m, but a cupboard {w} m by {h} m stands in one corner. How many square metres of the floor can be covered with carpet?
exercise: {a} has a sheet of card {W} cm by {H} cm. {a.He} cuts a {w} cm by {h} cm piece from one corner. What is the area of the card that is left, in square centimetres?
exercise: A rectangular pool {w} m by {h} m is built in the corner of a yard {W} m by {H} m. The rest of the yard is grass. How many square metres of grass are there?
test: The perimeter of an L-shaped yard is {2*(W+H)} m. The yard is a {W} m by {H} m rectangle with a {w} m by {h} m corner missing. What is its area in square metres?
test: Two rectangles are joined to make one shape: the first is {W-w} cm by {H} cm, the second is {w} cm by {H-h} cm. What area does the shape cover, in square centimetres?
test: How many square tiles, 1 m by 1 m, are needed to cover a floor shaped like a {W} m by {H} m rectangle without its {w} m by {h} m corner?
test: Two rectangles, {W} cm by {H-h} cm and {W-w} cm by {h} cm, are put together into an L. Find the area of the L in square centimetres.
exercise: What is the area, in square centimetres, of a rectangle {W} cm by {H} cm once a corner {w} cm by {h} cm is cut away?
exercise: A lawn in Ohio measures {W} m by {H} m, but a shed {w} m by {h} m takes up one corner. How many square metres of lawn are left?
exercise: {a} draws a rectangle {W} cm by {H} cm and rubs out a rectangle {w} cm by {h} cm in its corner. What area is left, in square centimetres?
exercise: An L-shaped kitchen floor in a house in Dublin is made of one part {W} m by {H-h} m and another part {W-w} m by {h} m. How many square metres is the floor?
exercise: A plot of land is two rectangles joined along a side: {W-w} m by {H} m and {w} m by {H-h} m. What is its total area in square metres?
exercise: A patio in Perth measures {W} m by {H} m and has a flower bed {w} m by {h} m in one corner. The rest is paved. How many square metres are paved?
exercise: Find the area of an L shape made by removing a rectangle {w} by {h} from the corner of a rectangle {W} by {H}, in square units.
exercise: A car park in Manchester, {W} m by {H} m, has a ticket booth {w} m by {h} m in one corner. How many square metres are left for cars?
test: In square metres, how big is a floor that is {W} m by {H} m except for a corner {w} m by {h} m taken up by the stairs?
test: Two rectangular rooms in a flat in London join to make an L: one is {W} m by {H-h} m, the other {W-w} m by {h} m. How many square metres of floor do they have together?
test: A board {W} cm by {H} cm has a notch {w} cm by {h} cm cut from one corner, and its perimeter is {2*(W+H)} cm. {a} paints the top of the board. How many square centimetres does {a.he} paint?
test: One rectangle is {w} cm wide and {H-h} cm tall; next to it stands a rectangle {W-w} cm wide and {H} cm tall. What is the area of the two together, in square centimetres?
test: How many 1 m by 1 m squares of turf cover a garden in Vancouver that is {W} m by {H} m, except for a corner {w} m by {h} m where a pond is?
test: From a rectangle {W} by {H}, take away a corner {w} by {h}. What area remains, in square units?
exercise: {W} by {H} cm card, cut a {w} by {h} bit off one corner. how much area left, square cm
