test: {a} reckons the area's {W*H} − {w} = {W*H-w}. wrong lol. {W} by {H} m garden with a {w} by {h} m corner taken out — how big really
exam: It is given that a rectangle measuring {w} cm by {h} cm is excised from one corner of a rectangle measuring {W} cm by {H} cm. Determine the area of the remaining figure, expressed in square centimetres.
exam: Whereas a rectangular sheet of {W} cm by {H} cm has had a rectangular portion of {w} cm by {h} cm removed from one of its corners, compute the area of the residual sheet in square centimetres.
exam: An L-shaped plot is constituted of two rectangles, the first measuring {W} m by {H-h} m and the second measuring {W-w} m by {h} m. Ascertain the aggregate area of the plot in square metres.
exam: State, in square metres, the area of a rectangular lawn of {W} m by {H} m that remains uncovered subsequent to the placement upon it of a rectangular flower bed of {w} m by {h} m.
exercise: The estate agent says the {W} m by {H} m plot is "full of character": a {w} m by {h} m corner of it belongs to the neighbour. How many square metres are really for sale?
exercise: The old shed gave up the ghost and was carted off from the corner of a {W} m by {H} m garden. It had stood on a {w} m by {h} m patch. How many square metres of the garden were not under the shed?
test: bloody carpet guy was creative with the truth, says {W*H} square metres. room's {W} by {H} m but there's a {w} by {h} m cupboard in the corner getting no carpet. how much carpet really, eh
